1.3 KUBERNETES - SCENARIO
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[QUESTION]
Create a Deployment named app-suite containing two containers (frontend: nginx, backend: python HTTP server) 
running 3 replicas, sharing a volume at /data, and exposed via ClusterIP service app-suite-svc on port 80.

[FILE: app-suite.yaml]
```yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: app-suite
spec:
  replicas: 3
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: app-suite
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: app-suite
    spec:
      volumes:
        - name: shared-data
          emptyDir: {}
      containers:
        - name: frontend
          image: nginx:alpine
          volumeMounts:
            - name: shared-data
              mountPath: /data
        - name: backend
          image: python:3.10-alpine
          command: ["python", "-m", "http.server", "5000"]
          volumeMounts:
            - name: shared-data
              mountPath: /data
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: app-suite-svc
spec:
  type: ClusterIP
  selector:
    app: app-suite
  ports:
    - port: 80
      targetPort: 80
```

[RUN COMMANDS]
kubectl apply -f app-suite.yaml
kubectl get pods
kubectl exec -it deployment/app-suite -c frontend -- ls /data
kubectl exec -it deployment/app-suite -c backend -- ls /data


