1.4 XML & XQUERY - SCENARIO
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[QUESTION]
Create hotel.xml and XQuery FLWOR and group-by expressions.

[FILE: hotel.xml]
```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<hotels>
    <hotel hotelID="H1">
        <name>Grand Hotel</name>
        <starValue>5</starValue>
        <phone>123456</phone>
        <address><street>Main St</street><pincode>10001</pincode></address>
        <website>grand.com</website>
        <departments deptID="D1">
            <department>
                <name>FrontOffice</name>
                <location><floor>1</floor><extension>101</extension></location>
            </department>
        </departments>
        <rooms>
            <room roomID="R1" type="Deluxe">
                <Roomtype>Deluxe</Roomtype>
                <rate>100</rate>
                <amenities><amenity><name>Wi-Fi</name></amenity></amenities>
            </room>
        </rooms>
    </hotel>
    <hotel hotelID="H2">
        <name>Star Inn</name>
        <starValue>3</starValue>
        <phone>654321</phone>
        <address><street>Park St</street><pincode>10002</pincode></address>
        <website>star.com</website>
        <departments deptID="D2">
            <department>
                <name>Housekeeping</name>
                <location><floor>0</floor><extension>102</extension></location>
            </department>
        </departments>
        <rooms>
            <room roomID="R2" type="Standard">
                <Roomtype>Standard</Roomtype>
                <rate>50</rate>
                <amenities><amenity><name>Breakfast</name></amenity></amenities>
            </room>
        </rooms>
    </hotel>
</hotels>
```

[FILE: queries.xq]
```xquery
(: Group by starValue :)
for $h in doc("hotel.xml")/hotels/hotel
group by $star := $h/starValue
return <group star="{$star}">{$h/name}</group>

(: FLWOR 5-Star Filter :)
for $h in doc("hotel.xml")/hotels/hotel
where $h/starValue = 5
return $h
```


